You are a senior full-stack engineer. Build a contract-first system for an “Issue & Solution Hub” as specified below. Do the work in this order:

A) Produce an OpenAPI 3.1 spec (openapi.yaml)

Use title: IssueSolutionHub API

Version: 1.0.0

Servers: http://localhost:8080

Schemas (match exactly unless you propose improvements with comments):

User { id: UUID, displayName, email, createdAt }

Issue { id, title*, description, urgency (0–100), firstReportedDate, problemStartDate?, problemStartIsFuture (bool), counterpointNotes, similarityCount (int, readOnly), resolvesCount (int, readOnly), uniqueSupportersInTree (int, readOnly), createdByUserId, createdAt, updatedAt, categories: string[], tags: string[] }

IssueCreateRequest { title*, description, urgency*, firstReportedDate*, problemStartDate?, problemStartIsFuture?, counterpointNotes?, categories?, tags? }

IssueSearchQuery { text?, categories?, tags?, urgencyMin?, urgencyMax?, sortBy? = ["MOST_URGENT","MOST_UPVOTED","MOST_SIMILAR","NEWEST","HIGHEST_RESOLVES"] , page?, pageSize? }

IssueListItem (subset for lists) { id, title, urgency, localUpvotesCount, similarityCount, resolvesCount, uniqueSupportersInTree, categories, tags, createdAt }

IssueDetail extends Issue plus: localUpvotesCount (int, readOnly), parentId?, children: IssueListItem[], similarIssues: SimilarIssue[], linkedSolutions: PotentialSolutionLink[]

SimilarIssue { issue: IssueListItem, similarityScore (0..1), status: ["SUGGESTED","CONFIRMED","REJECTED"], differenceSummary? }

PotentialSolution { id, title*, summary, estimatedCost: { amount: number, currency: "USD"|"EUR"|string }, timeToDeliver: { unit: "days"|"weeks"|"months", value: int }, resourcesNeeded: string[], estimatedTimeSavedPerPeriod: { unit: "minutes_per_week"|"hours_per_week", value: int }, valueAddNotes, createdByUserId, createdAt, updatedAt }

PotentialSolutionCreateRequest same fields minus IDs/readonly

PotentialSolutionLink { solutionId, rank?, notes? }

UpvoteRequest { userId }

SimilarityCheckResponse { similarIssues: SimilarIssue[] }

CheckAndMaybeCreateResponse { created?: IssueDetail, similarIssues?: SimilarIssue[] } // if similar above threshold, do NOT create; else return created

Standard Problem for errors.

Paths (define request/response bodies, params, and examples):

POST /issues:checkAndMaybeCreate — body: IssueCreateRequest; returns CheckAndMaybeCreateResponse

POST /issues — direct create (bypass check); returns IssueDetail

GET /issues — query via IssueSearchQuery (query params); returns { items: IssueListItem[], page, pageSize, total }

GET /issues/{id} — returns IssueDetail

POST /issues/{id}/upvotes — body: UpvoteRequest; returns { localUpvotesCount, uniqueSupportersInTree }

POST /issues/{id}/sub-issues — body: IssueCreateRequest + differenceSummary (string); creates a child AND a SimilarityLink with status=CONFIRMED; returns the new child IssueDetail

GET /issues/{id}/similar — returns SimilarityCheckResponse

POST /issues/{id}/solutions — body: PotentialSolutionLink; links existing solution, returns updated IssueDetail

DELETE /issues/{id}/solutions/{solutionId} — unlink

POST /solutions — create PotentialSolution

GET /solutions — list with basic filters

GET /solutions/{id} — detail

POST /issues/{id}/categories — body: { categories: string[] } (curated names)

POST /issues/{id}/tags — body: { tags: string[] } (freeform, normalize lower-case)

GET /categories — list curated categories

Components:

